---
title: 'Text Test'
---

These examples stress-test `block: true` image segments across every context that accepts rich-text
segment arrays (`ContentSegment[]`): captions, axis labels and series labels. The goal is to surface
layout and positioning issues early, so each example packs in as many edge cases as possible. A block
image anchors to the left of a layout row while text flows into the column to its right; multiple
block rows stack vertically.

## Captions — content variety

What to test:

- Two stacked block rows in the title (block, text, `\n`, block, text) with decorated block images.
- A block image followed by an inline image in the subtitle.
- An oversized block image in the footnote is dropped under the default `hide` strategy while the text
  still renders.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Images in Captions" name="block-captions" type="generated" /%}

## Captions — alignment

What to test:

- The same block-leading content rendered with `textAlign` left, center and right.
- Block rows stay left-anchored within the caption box while single lines follow the alignment.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Image Caption Alignment" name="block-caption-alignment" type="generated" /%}

## Axis labels — both axes

What to test:

- An x category axis whose labels are a block image, the category text, and a trailing inline marker.
- A y number axis whose labels are a block image followed by the value.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Images in Axis Labels" name="block-axis-labels" type="generated" /%}

## Axis labels — rotated

What to test:

- Long category labels rotated 45°, each with a leading block icon, laid out without overlap or
  clipping.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Rotated Block Image Axis Labels" name="block-axis-rotated" type="generated" /%}

## Series labels — arrangement matrix

What to test (one edge case per tile):

- Leading block; two stacked block rows; a trailing block kept inline (no `\n`); two and three
  side-by-side blocks; block + inline mix; tall image with `verticalAlign` top/bottom; asymmetric
  padding + background fill; border + radius; an oversized image dropped under `hide`; and a long
  label wrapping into the narrow column.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Image Arrangement Matrix" name="block-treemap-arrangements" type="generated" /%}

## Series labels — heatmap

What to test:

- Block image labels inside small heatmap cells, exercising tight label boxes.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Images in Heatmap Cells" name="block-heatmap" type="generated" /%}

## Series labels — sunburst

What to test:

- Block image labels inside sunburst slices of varying angular width.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Block Images in Sunburst Slices" name="block-sunburst" type="generated" /%}
